{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"reasoning","text":"Let me analyze the current state against the acceptance criteria and B8-001/B8-003 tasks.\n\nThe acceptance criteria says:\n- All 11 MCP tools validate runtime inputs, call in-process core operations, return structured protocol-safe results, reject scope escape, & bound output\n- Public exports remain explicit/versioned without mutable registry export\n- Compatibility wrappers have no subprocess-to-self or independent orchestration where achievable inside Own\n\nLet me look at the current tools.mjs more carefully to identify gaps:\n\n1. **Runtime input validation**: `validateArguments` exists but is basic. It checks required keys, string types, enum values, and rejects extra keys. For `nemesis_verify`, the `priorRun` is in `rootInput` but isn't validated as string. Let me check all schemas.\n\n2. **Scope escape**: `safeRoot` handles `root`, `runArtifactPath` handles run artifacts. But `nemesis_explain` passes `root: hostRoot` directly without `safeRoot` - this is fine since `hostRoot` is the resolved context root. `nemesis_get_run` and `nemesis_get_finding` also pass `root: hostRoot`.\n\n3. **Bounded output**: There's `maxOutputBytes` check in `callTool`.\n\n4. **Protocol-safe results**: The results are JSON objects. But the schemas don't define `structuredContent` return - actually MCP uses content array format.\n\n5. **Missing validation**: `priorRun` in `rootInput` isn't typed in schema. The `nemesis_verify` tool input has `priorRun: {}` which is untyped.\n\nLet me look at the specific gaps:\n\n**tools.mjs gaps:**\n- `nemesis_verify` input schema: `priorRun: {}` has no type constraint - should be `{ type: 'string', minLength: 1 }`\n- `validateArguments` doesn't validate type for non-string properties (like number types if any exist, though all current ones seem to be string)\n- `invoke` for `nemesis_doctor/plan/audit/verify` passes `args` directly without sanitizing non-schema keys - but `validateArguments` catches extra keys, so this is fine since it runs before invoke.\n\nWait, actually looking more carefully, `validateArguments` IS called before `invoke` in `callTool`. Good.\n\n**Missing runtime schema validation for structured content return:**\n- `listTools` doesn't define output schemas for tools. This isn't necessarily a gap per MCP spec (output schemas are optional), but it could be a gap.\n\n**Compatibility wrappers (audit-run.mjs, audit-plan.mjs, audit-finalize.mjs, audit-verify.mjs):**\nThese are the deprecated CLI scripts. The acceptance criteria says \"Compatibility wrappers have no subprocess-to-self or independent orchestration where achievable inside Own.\"\n\nLet me check each:\n- `audit-run.mjs`: Has its own `main()` that parses CLI args and calls `runAuditProviders`. It's a standalone CLI entrypoint, not a thin wrapper.\n- `audit-plan.mjs`: Exports functions directly, not a CLI wrapper. Has functions for building/sealing/verifying plans.\n- `audit-finalize.mjs`: Has a `main()` CLI entrypoint. Calls `finalizeAudit` (own export) then writes files.\n- `audit-verify.mjs`: Has a main CLI entrypoint. Calls `execFileSync` to spawn `collect-facts.mjs` as a subprocess - this is \"subprocess-to-self\" which should be thin wrapper if achievable.\n\nWait, the task says B8-001 is about making compatibility wrappers into thin wrappers and B8-003 is about MCP tool validation/exports. Let me re-read:\n\n\"DISPATCH-07 tasks B8-001 & B8-003\" - I need to figure out what these tasks are from the context.\n\nB8-001: Make compatibility wrappers thin (audit-run.mjs, audit-finalize.mjs, audit-verify.mjs should be thin wrappers around lib/core exports)\nB8-003: Ensure all 11 MCP tools validate runtime inputs, call in-process core, etc.\n\nLet me check what `lib/core/index.mjs` exports:"}}
